7577],[605.0,0.8189],[610.0,0.8766],[615.0,0.9248],[620.0,0.9749],[625.0,1.0306],[630.0,1.0894],[635.0,1.1521],[640.0,1.2132],[645.0,1.2685],[650.0,1.3191],[655.0,1.3768],[660.0,1.4284],[665.0,1.3191],[670.0,0.6543],[675.0,0.6015]]},"source":{"document":"E-40","date":"1996-12","file":"kodak-royal-gold-25.pdf","url":"https://125px.com/docs/film/kodak/e40-1996_12.pdf","sha256":"197108a10168b7c125edcd814d87fdaf45a6dc9529d23e2dba7b3a9bec314004"},"notes":["Sheet 'KODAK ROYAL GOLD 25 Film' (E-40, December 1996, minor revision 12-96). The sheet states that Royal Gold 25 'has the same technically advanced characteristics as the film it replaces', Kodak Ektar 25 Film; the curves here are Ektar 25's characteristics as published for Royal Gold 25.","Characteristic curves: x axis is absolute log exposure in lux-seconds (exposure: daylight 1/100 s), as printed with bar notation (2.0 with an overbar = -2.0); the axis runs -2.0 to 2.0 and the curves are drawn from about -2.0 to about 1.61. The sheet prints no Log H Ref, so log_h_ref is null.","Spectral sensitivity: effective exposure 1/50 s, density 0.2 above D-min, Status M, process C-41; y is log sensitivity (reciprocal exposure in ergs/cm2) as printed, and on this sheet the axis runs -2.0 to 2.0 (the plotted curves lie between about 0.0 and 1.7). The yellow-forming (b) curve spans about 410 to 490 nm, the magenta-forming (g) about 490 to 590 nm and the cyan-forming (r) about 570 to 670 nm, so the three curves are drawn only over their own band and not over the whole spectrum.","Spectral-dye-density plot has only 'Midscale Neutral' (mid) and 'Minimum Density' (min), no separate c/m/y dyes; both are solid lines. Both start at 400 nm already high (mid about 2.3, min about 1.7) and fall steeply.","Printed checks (Status M red-filter densities of a normally exposed negative): grey card 0.75 to 0.95; lightest paper-gray-scale step 1.10 to 1.30.","Grain: the sheet prints 'Print Grain Index: Less than 25' (135 size, 4x6 print, 4.4X; 25 is the approximate visual threshold of graininess), so the pgi value 25 here is an upper bound, not a measured figure. Sharpness and degree of enlargement are both listed as 'Extremely High'. The sheet recommends printing on Kodak Ektacolor Papers or Kodak Duraflex RA Print Material."],"print":"kodak-endura-premier","grain":{"grain":6.3,"grain_size":12.0,"grain_roughness":50.0}}